INSERT INTO dcp_clause_sibling_citations (council, chapter_key, section_ref, sibling_chapter_key, sibling_section_ref,
    sibling_pdf_page, sibling_excerpt, verified_note)
VALUES ($sib$wingecarribee$sib$, $sib$wingecarribee-bowral-town-plan$sib$, $sib$part-c-s3/C3.8.2(c)$sib$, $sib$wingecarribee-mittagong-town-plan$sib$,
    $sib$part-c-s3/C3.8.2(c)$sib$, 206,
    $sib$MITTAGONG TOWN PLAN DCP PART C RESIDENTIAL ZONED LAND SECTION 3 MEDIUM DENSITY DEVELOPMENT Mittagong Town Plan – Effective 17 June 2015 PART C | Page 202 of 319 Due to the variety of front setbacks contributing to existing streetscapes, this Plan uses a contextual approach to establish front setbacks. New development should adopt front setbacks similar to those of existing adjacent dwellings, or of relevance in the immediate vicinity. C3.8.1 Objectives The controls described below are intended to achieve the following objectives: (a) Ensure the front setback of new infill development is consistent with the existing streetscape. (b) Preserve existing vegetation in front gardens. (c) Provide areas for trees and vegetation to enhance the streetscape and provide privacy. C3.8.2 Specific Controls (a) Front setbacks of new development will be consistent with those of the dwellings immediately adjacent to the site and to those in the immediate vicinity. (b) Where properties immediately adjacent to the proposed development do not feature a consistent front setback: (i) If the difference between existing front setbacks is 2 metres or greater, new dwellings can adopt a setback within the range established by adjacent dwellings; (ii) If the difference between existing front setbacks is greater than 2 metres, the new dwellings will adopt an average of the existing setbacks; (c) In the case where there are inconsistent setbacks immediately adjacent to the site, or in the immediate vicinity of the proposed development, or there are no dwellings immediately adjacent to, or in the vicinity of the proposed development, Council will assess the proposed front setback on merit. To date, the accepted standard has been 8 metres. (d) Secondary setbacks on corner blocks will be the subject of a contextual approach and will generally be half the requirement of the primary setback. (e) Proposals that seek to vary the front setback controls may do so only if it can be demonstrated to the satisfaction of Council that the proposed variation: (i) will enhance the quality of the existing streetscape, and (ii) will not compromise amenity of the any proposed or existing dwellings immediately adjacent to the proposed development. (f) Where it is common practice in the streetscape to have some variation in the alignment of the front setback, new development should reflect this pattern.$sib$,
    $sib$Located 2026-09-15 in our R2 copy of the Mittagong Town Plan (as amended 17 Jun 2015) (sha256 510613c46ede): clause C3.8.2 starts on page 206; every number of served control(s) [1158] ([Decimal('8.0')]) is printed on page 206.$sib$)
ON CONFLICT (council, chapter_key, section_ref, sibling_chapter_key) DO NOTHING;

